Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-n61: Enable the display pipe

The iPhone 6's display pipe and display DART are the iPod touch 6's.
Read from its Apple device tree (iOS 12.4, 16G77, n61ap), disp0 is
"adbe0,t7000" with the same windows (0x206200000 and the four 0x8000
blocks), interrupts (103, 108-111), power gate (112) and clock gates
(112, 118, 116); dart-disp0 has the same windows, interrupts (106, 107),
error reflector (0x20ffff000), fetch and diag configuration and gate
(36); and the panel link is the same two-lane mipi-dsim (0x206600000,
gate 113) with an "lcd,pinot" panel whose supply is on the display PMU.
So t7000.dtsi's description holds, and disp0 only needs enabling, as on
the iPod touch 6. dart-disp0 stays disabled: the display driver enables
it after mapping the live scanout.

What differs from the iPod touch 6, read from the ADT: two LM3534
backlight controllers (i2c0 and i2c1), a display EEPROM (i2c2, 0x51) and
a SAC memory range on mipi-dsim. None of them is touched by the display
pipe's driver. The 750x1334 panel mode is not in the ADT (iBoot fills in
the timing); the driver takes it from the boot framebuffer, so that size
is inferred from the iPhone 6's panel, not read.

Not run on an iPhone 6 yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
index 082ed32..efbeb6a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n61.dts
@@ -60,3 +60,11 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The display pipe takes the 750x1334 MIPI DSI panel over from simpledrm.
+ * No panel supply is given: the panel stays on in system sleep.
+ */
+&disp0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
